<title>JAPAN: Yaohan Japan falls sharply in Tokyo.</title>
<headline>Yaohan Japan falls sharply in Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yaohan Japan Corp fell sharply on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on Thursday due to uncertainties over how it will finance the redemption of convertible bonds due next year, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;How the company is going to finance the redemption is not yet clear, so investors are staying away from Yaohan shares,&quot; said a trader at a second-tier brokerage.</p>
<p>Yaohan was down 44 yen at 371 by 0502 GMT. It was the second-most heavily traded issue on the exchange with turnover of 4.65 million shares.</p>
</text>
